  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "r0q0j6a",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "INTRODUCTION TO ECONOMIC PLANNING"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Economic planning in India officially began with the First Five-Year Plan covering the period from 1951 to 1956.",
        "The planned trajectory faced an interruption known as the Plan Holiday from 1966 to 1969.",
        "The Twelfth Five-Year Plan (2012–2017) marked the final Five-Year Plan structure in India.",
        "NITI Aayog replaced the central planning framework starting in 2015 to direct national economic strategy."
      ],
      "id": "1tehdab"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "First FYP Era",
          "value": "1951–1956",
          "icon": "calendar"
        },
        {
          "label": "Plan Holiday",
          "value": "1966–1969",
          "icon": "clock"
        },
        {
          "label": "Final FYP Era",
          "value": "2012–2017",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "NITI Aayog",
          "value": "2015–Present",
          "icon": "award"
        }
      ],
      "id": "y5rlbio"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p13q5lw",
      "content": "Economic Planning refers to the conscious and systematic effort made by the government to use national resources efficiently to achieve economic and social goals within a fixed period."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2le9ebc",
      "content": "It answers four basic questions:"
    },
    {
      "id": "2bfwpk5",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "What to produce?",
        "How much to produce?",
        "How to produce?",
        "For whom to produce?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "q520wyg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "NEED FOR ECONOMIC PLANNING IN INDIA"
